Package: hyprland-static
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: heisenagent <297739722+heisenagent@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Recommends: hyprland, xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland, xwayland
Suggests: hyprlock, hypridle, hyprpolkitagent, waybar
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/heisenagent/hyprland-static
Description: Hyprland built with statically linked Hyprland libraries
 A newer Hyprland than the Ubuntu LTS release ships, built against that
 release.  Hyprland's own libraries (hyprutils, hyprlang, hyprwire,
 hyprgraphics, hyprcursor, aquamarine) are linked statically, so it doesn't
 replace or conflict with Ubuntu's packages.
 .
 Installs into /opt/hyprland-static and adds a "Hyprland (static)" entry to
 the login screen.  Ubuntu's hyprland package (recommended) stays available
 as a fallback session and provides the desktop portal configuration.  Also
 includes brightnessctl built with logind support, so brightness keys work
 without membership in the "video" group.
